course: dictionary
lesson: 6637
title: Nowhere: not in any place
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Nowhere» means not in any place, or not to any place. If your bag is nowhere to be found, you cannot find it in any place at all. Try it in a sentence: «Steam in a bathroom with no window has nowhere to go» means the steam has no place to go.
explain: The second meaning is about a place far from towns. «In the middle of nowhere» means a lonely spot with nothing near it. Good to know for safety: if you are lost in the middle of nowhere, stay where you are so people can find you.
explain: «Out of nowhere» is a phrase that means suddenly, with no warning. When you meet a new phrase, check the words around it. The clues tell you which meaning fits.
fact: «Nowhere» can be an adverb or a pronoun.
fact: «Nowhere» means not in any place, or not to any place.
fact: «In the middle of nowhere» means far from towns, with nothing near.
fact: «Out of nowhere» means suddenly, with no warning.
fact: «Nowhere else» means in no other place, as in fish «found nowhere else» in the Congo River.
exercise: «The Congo River has more than seven hundred kinds of fish, many found nowhere else.» What does nowhere else mean here? | Very often | In the next river | At the bottom of the sea | *In no other place
exercise: Maya says the lost walker is «in the middle of nowhere». What does this mean? | Very close to a shop | *Far from towns, with nothing near | Lost in a crowded city | Hiding in a cupboard
exercise: If you are lost in the middle of nowhere, what should you do? | Walk until you find a town | *Stay where you are so people can find you | Run as fast as you can in any direction | Climb the highest tree you can see
test: «The password is written nowhere online.» What does nowhere mean here? | *Not in any place online | On the first page | In every place online | Somewhere very fast
test: Ella says her phone rang «out of nowhere». What does out of nowhere mean? | Slowly, after a long wait | *Suddenly, with no warning | In a cupboard | From a far-away town
exam: Which phrase means far from towns, with nothing near? | *In the middle of nowhere | Out of nowhere | Nowhere near | Nowhere else
